WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.030
«Je fais mes devoirs.» I do my homework.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.580
Simple. Now put three
small words in front:

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.340
«Il faut que je fasse
mes devoirs.» Same verb.

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:14.030
Same person. But «fais»
has turned into «fasse».

5
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:17.540
Why would a few words in
front change a verb's form?

6
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:19.870
And what does the sentence mean now?

7
00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:22.740
In this mission, you'll flip
the switch on that verb,

8
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.730
and meet the words that pull it.

9
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.900
Then you'll trace odd-looking forms
back to verbs you already know.

10
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.870
Your mission: find out
what flips the switch,

11
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.190
and how to read the sentence once it has.
